Let $x$ be the number of three-point shots Shenille made and $y$ be the number of two-point shots she made.
We are given that she made 20% of her three-point shots, so $0.2x$ three-point shots were successful.
Similarly, she made 30% of her two-point shots, so $0.3y$ two-point shots were successful.
We can set up a system of equations:
\begin{align*}
x + y &= 30 \\
0.2x + 0.3y &= \text{total points}
\end{align*}
Since each three-point shot is worth 3 points and each two-point shot is worth 2 points, the total points can be expressed as $3(0.2x) + 2(0.3y)$.
Simplifying, we have:
\begin{align*}
x + y &= 30 \\
0.6x + 0.6y &= \text{total points}
\end{align*}
Substituting $30 - x$ for $y$ in the second equation, we have:
\begin{align*}
0.6x + 0.6(30 - x) &= \text{total points} \\
0.6x + 18 - 0.6x &= \text{total points} \\
18 &= \text{total points}
\end{align*}
Therefore, Shenille scored $\boxed{18}$ points.
The answer is: 18

